{%- comment -%}
  PG Gift Guard: owns the free case, and badges it only when a console earns it.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- background
  The case product used to have one "Default Title" variant at $13.99
  (49623692247268), zeroed by the "Free R36S Case with Console" BXGY. Two
  problems with that: the BXGY consumed the single automatic-discount slot
  Shopify allows per order, so no per-product bundle ladder could apply
  alongside it; and the ID was hardcoded in pg-drawer's giftSync.

  The product now carries two real variants:

      49640846426340  $0.00   "Free with console"   -> the gift
      49640879063268  $13.99  "Spare case"          -> the paid upsell

  Adding the named variant replaced the old default one, so 49623692247268 is
  gone and giftSync's add now 422s -- it can no longer place the gift. This
  section takes that job over. The gift is free because it is priced at zero,
  which also leaves the discount slot free for a bundle ladder.

  giftSync's OTHER behaviours still work and are deliberately left alone: it
  finds the gift line by product handle (both variants share it), so it still
  removes the gift when the cart empties of consoles, and still moves surplus
  units off the badged line.

  ================================================================
  THE CART FILLING UP WITH CASES

  Reported: a few seconds after the Duo Pack goes in, the drawer starts
  rebuilding itself over and over and more cases keep arriving. This file was
  the source, and the chain is worth writing down because two other sections
  are downstream of it.

  ensureGift() used to ask "does any line carry the _free_gift property?" and
  add a gift when the answer was no. That question is not the same as "is the
  gift already in the cart", and it is answered from a /cart.js read that can
  be stale: the drawer, pg-cart-variants, pg-cart-total, pg-chips and this
  file all poll that endpoint, and under that load Shopify starts throttling
  it -- pg-chips documents responses coming back unparseable for exactly this
  reason. One stale answer and this file adds a SECOND gift. The add merges
  into the same line, so the gift line's quantity becomes 2.

  Downstream, two separate sections watch for precisely that:

      pg-drawer     giftSync()  : gift.quantity > 1 -> set it to 1, then
                                  ADD the surplus as 49640879063268
      pg-case-mobile normalise(): the same rule, on its own 2s beat

  So one stale read turns into a $13.99 spare case the shopper never asked
  for; each of those writes refreshes the drawer; each refresh is more load on
  the same endpoint, and the next stale read does it again. That is the cart
  "glitching out and adding more cases", and every case it added was billable.

  THREE CHANGES, ALL HERE, so no other file has to be touched:

  1. The gift is detected BY VARIANT, not by a property. 49640846426340 in the
     cart means the gift is present, whatever its properties say and whoever
     put it there. A question that cannot go stale into a false "no".
  2. An add is followed by a cooldown, and re-checked against a fresh read
     before it can happen again. A slow endpoint can no longer be answered
     with a second gift.
  3. The gift line is CAPPED at one unit here, by removal. It is capped in
     pg-drawer and pg-case-mobile too, but both do it by moving the surplus
     onto the paid variant -- i.e. by charging for it. Removing the surplus
     first means their branch has nothing left to sell. A unit that arrived by
     accident is not an upsell.

  The read beat is also slowed from 1.2s to 2s. The badge pass stays at 250ms:
  it touches the DOM only and never the network.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the badge
  giftTag() picks the line to badge in this order: the line Shopify discounted
  to zero, else the line carrying _free_gift, else -- as a "never show nothing"
  fallback -- the first case line on screen. That fallback is wrong on its own:
  a spare case bought with no console hits exactly that state and gets badged
  FREE GIFT while being charged for, with its stepper and remove button hidden
  by pg-drawer's `li:has(.pg-free-tag)` rules. This strips the badge whenever
  the cart has not earned a gift, stamping data-pg-free so giftTag() treats the
  line as handled and does not put it back.

  DEPLOY NOTE: the live theme still references the dead variant, so its free
  case is broken until this theme is published. Publish, verify a console adds
  a $0.00 case, and only then disable the "Free R36S Case with Console"
  discount -- it is now redundant, but harmless while it stays on.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftGuard) return; window.pgGiftGuard = 1;

  var CASE_LINK = 'free-gift';               /* the case handle ends in -free-gift */
  var CONSOLE_HANDLE = 'handheld-game-console';
  var FREE_VARIANT = 49640846426340;         /* $0.00 "Free with console" */
  var LINES = '#cart .l4ca > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li';
  /* null = not checked yet. The badge is only ever removed on an explicit
     false, so a failed or pending /cart.js never blanks a legitimate gift. */
  var earned = null;
  var busy = false;
  var adding = false;
  /* No add may follow another inside this window, however many reads come back
     saying the cart is empty of gifts. 8s comfortably outlasts a throttled
     response and every drawer refresh it can trigger. */
  var COOLDOWN = 8000;
  var lastAdd = 0;
  var capping = false;

  function caseLines(){
    var out = [];
    document.querySelectorAll(LINES).forEach(function(li){
      if (li.querySelector('a[href*="' + CASE_LINK + '"]')) out.push(li);
    });
    return out;
  }

  function apply(){
    var lis = caseLines();
    if (!lis.length) return;
    if (earned === false){
      lis.forEach(function(li){
        li.dataset.pgFree = '1';
        li.querySelectorAll('.pg-free-tag').forEach(function(el){ el.parentNode.removeChild(el); });
      });
    } else if (earned === true){
      /* A line marked as handled but wearing no badge is one this guard
         cleared earlier. Release it so pg-drawer can badge it again now that
         the cart qualifies. */
      lis.forEach(function(li){
        if (li.dataset.pgFree && !li.querySelector('.pg-free-tag')) delete li.dataset.pgFree;
      });
    }
  }

  /* The gift line, BY VARIANT. Properties are how this file marks its own
     work, not how the cart is read back: a line can be rebuilt, merged or
     re-added by another section and lose the marker while still being the
     free case sitting in the shopper's cart. */
  function giftLine(cart){
    var found = null;
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (it.variant_id === FREE_VARIANT) found = it;
    });
    return found;
  }

  /* Place the gift ourselves: giftSync's hardcoded variant no longer exists.
     Guarded three ways -- an in-flight add, a cooldown, and a fresh read taken
     at the moment of the decision -- because the read that got us here may be
     older than the last add. */
  function ensureGift(cart){
    if (adding) return;
    if (Date.now() - lastAdd < COOLDOWN) return;
    var items = cart.items || [];
    if (!items.some(function(it){ return it.handle === CONSOLE_HANDLE; })) return;
    if (giftLine(cart)) return;
    adding = true;
    /* one more read, taken now: the cart above may predate an add that has
       already landed, and adding a second gift is the whole bug */
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(fresh){
        if (giftLine(fresh) || !(fresh.items || []).some(function(it){ return it.handle === CONSOLE_HANDLE; })){
          adding = false;
          return;
        }
        lastAdd = Date.now();
        return fetch('/cart/add.js', {
          method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
          body: JSON.stringify({items: [{id: FREE_VARIANT, quantity: 1, properties: {_free_gift: 'yes'}}]})
        }).then(function(r){
          adding = false;
          if (!r.ok) return;
          if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
        });
      })
      .catch(function(){ adding = false; });
  }

  /* One free case, never more. pg-drawer and pg-case-mobile both answer a
     surplus here by selling it as a $13.99 spare; taking it off first leaves
     them nothing to sell. Removal only, and only ever of the $0.00 variant --
     a spare the shopper actually chose is a different variant and is never
     touched. */
  function capGift(cart){
    if (capping || adding) return;
    var gift = giftLine(cart);
    if (!gift || gift.quantity <= 1) return;
    capping = true;
    fetch('/cart/change.js', {
      method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      credentials: 'same-origin',
      body: JSON.stringify({id: gift.key, quantity: 1})
    }).then(function(){
      capping = false;
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
    }).catch(function(){ capping = false; });
  }

  function check(){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(c){
        earned = (c.items || []).some(function(it){
          return it.handle === CONSOLE_HANDLE || (it.properties && it.properties._free_gift);
        });
        busy = false;
        apply();
        capGift(c);
        ensureGift(c);
      })
      .catch(function(){ busy = false; });
  }

  /* apply() is cheap and runs often so the badge never lingers between cart
     reads; check() re-reads the cart on a slower beat -- slower than it was,
     because this endpoint is shared with four other sections and throttles
     under the load they were putting on it together. */
  setInterval(apply, 250);
  setInterval(check, 2000);
  check();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Gift Guard", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
